{"id":"mahabharata-8-030","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":30,"title":"त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 30 · Karna insults the Madras","summary":{"en":"Karna, angry at Shalya's mockery, speaks scornfully of the Madra and Bahlika peoples, recalling their faults and customs and saying their women are unchaste. Shalya says nothing to this and smiles, and the chariot goes on.","kn":"ಶಲ್ಯನ ಗೇಲಿಯಿಂದ ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಕರ್ಣ ಮದ್ರ, ಬಾಹ್ಲೀಕರ ದೋಷ, ಆಚಾರಗಳನ್ನು ತಿರಸ್ಕಾರದಿಂದ ಹೇಳಿ ಅವರ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು ಶೀಲಹೀನರೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಲ್ಯ ಉತ್ತರಿಸದೆ ನಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಥ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"शल्य के उपहास से क्रुद्ध कर्ण मद्र और बाह्लीक जनों की निन्दा करता है, उनके दोष और रीतियाँ गिनाता है और उनकी स्त्रियों को अशुद्ध कहता है। शल्य कुछ नहीं कहता और मुस्कुराता है, और रथ आगे बढ़ता है।","te":"శల్యుని ఎగతాళికి కోపించిన కర్ణుడు మద్ర, బాహ్లీక జనులను తిరస్కారంగా మాట్లాడి వారి దోషాలను, ఆచారాలను చెప్పి వారి స్త్రీలు శీలహీనులంటాడు. శల్యుడు ఏమీ అనకుండా నవ్వుతాడు; రథం సాగుతుంది.","ta":"சல்யனின் கேலியால் சினமுற்ற கர்ணன் மத்ர, பாஹ்லீக மக்களை இகழ்ந்து அவர்களின் குறைகளையும் வழக்கங்களையும் கூறி அவர்கள் பெண்கள் ஒழுக்கமற்றோர் என்கிறான். சல்யன் எதுவும் கூறாது சிரிக்க, தேர் முன்னேறுகிறது.","ml":"ശല്യന്റെ പരിഹാസത്തിൽ കോപിച്ച കർണ്ണൻ, മദ്രരെയും ബാഹ്ലികരെയും കുറിച്ച് നിന്ദയോടെ സംസാരിക്കുന്നു; അവരുടെ കുറവുകളും ആചാരങ്ങളും ഓർത്ത്, അവരുടെ സ്ത്രീകൾ ചാരിത്ര്യമില്ലാത്തവരാണെന്ന് പറയുന്നു. ശല്യൻ ഒന്നും മിണ്ടാതെ പുഞ്ചിരിക്കുന്നു; രഥം മുന്നോട്ടുതന്നെ പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.30; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः पुनर्महाराज मद्रराजमरिंदमम् ।\nअभ्यभाषत राधेयः संनिवार्योत्तरं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, Radheya, having checked Shalya, the subduer of foes, spoke again to the king of Madra."}},{"n":2,"text":"यत्त्वं निदर्शनार्थं मां शल्य जल्पितवानसि ।\nनाहं शक्यस्त्वया वाचा विभीषयितुमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, you have spoken by way of illustration, but you cannot frighten me in battle with words."}},{"n":3,"text":"यदि मां देवताः सर्वा योधयेयुः सवासवाः ।\nतथापि मे भयं न स्यात्किमु पार्थात्सकेशवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if all the gods with Indra fought me, I would feel no fear; how much less of Partha with Keshava."}},{"n":4,"text":"नाहं भीषयितुं शक्यो वाङ्मात्रेण कथंचन ।\nअन्यं जानीहि यः शक्यस्त्वया भीषयितुं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot be frightened by mere words in any way. Know that you may frighten someone else in battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"नीचस्य बलमेतावत्पारुष्यं यत्त्वमात्थ माम् ।\nअशक्तोऽस्मद्गुणान्प्राप्तुं वल्गसे बहु दुर्मते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This harshness you show me is the strength of a low man; unable to reach our qualities, you rant much, wicked one."}},{"n":6,"text":"न हि कर्णः समुद्भूतो भयार्थमिह मारिष ।\nविक्रमार्थमहं जातो यशोर्थं च तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, sir, was not born here for fear. I was born for valor and likewise for fame."}},{"n":7,"text":"इदं तु मे त्वमेकाग्रः शृणु मद्रजनाधिप ।\nसंनिधौ धृतराष्ट्रस्य प्रोच्यमानं मया श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now listen with full attention, lord of the Madras, to something I heard said in Dhritarashtra's presence."}},{"n":8,"text":"देशांश्च विविधांश्चित्रान्पूर्ववृत्तांश्च पार्थिवान् ।\nब्राह्मणाः कथयन्तः स्म धृतराष्ट्रमुपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins used to attend Dhritarashtra, telling of various wondrous lands and of kings of former times."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्र वृद्धः पुरावृत्ताः कथाः काश्चिद्द्विजोत्तमः ।\nबाह्लीकदेशं मद्रांश्च कुत्सयन्वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There an aged, excellent brahmin told some tales of the past, and, scorning the Bahlika country and the Madras, he spoke these words."}},{"n":10,"text":"बहिष्कृता हिमवता गङ्गया च तिरस्कृताः ।\nसरस्वत्या यमुनया कुरुक्षेत्रेण चापि ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are outside the Himalaya, shunned by the Ganga, the Sarasvati, the Yamuna and Kurukshetra,"}},{"n":11,"text":"पञ्चानां सिन्धुषष्ठानां नदीनां येऽन्तराश्रिताः ।\nतान्धर्मबाह्यानशुचीन्बाह्लीकान्परिवर्जयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"who live between the five rivers with the Sindhu as the sixth: those Bahlikas, outside dharma and impure, should be avoided."}},{"n":12,"text":"गोवर्धनो नाम वटः सुभाण्डं नाम चत्वरम् ।\nएतद्राजकुलद्वारमाकुमारः स्मराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A banyan called Govardhana and a square called Subhanda: these, the gate of the royal house, I have remembered since boyhood."}},{"n":13,"text":"कार्येणात्यर्थगाढेन बाह्लीकेषूषितं मया ।\nतत एषां समाचारः संवासाद्विदितो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"On some very urgent business I lived among the Bahlikas, and from living there I learned their conduct."}},{"n":14,"text":"शाकलं नाम नगरमापगा नाम निम्नगा ।\nजर्तिका नाम बाह्लीकास्तेषां वृत्तं सुनिन्दितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a city called Shakala and a river called Apaga; the Bahlikas called Jartikas have a most blameworthy way of life."}},{"n":15,"text":"धानागौडासवे पीत्वा गोमांसं लशुनैः सह ।\nअपूपमांसवाट्यानामाशिनः शीलवर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They drink liquor made of grain and molasses, eat beef with garlic, and eat cakes, meat and fried food, without good conduct."}},{"n":16,"text":"हसन्ति गान्ति नृत्यन्ति स्त्रीभिर्मत्ता विवाससः ।\nनगरागारवप्रेषु बहिर्माल्यानुलेपनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drunk, they laugh, sing and dance with women, naked, wearing garlands and ointments, in the city, houses and ramparts, or outside."}},{"n":17,"text":"मत्तावगीतैर्विविधैः खरोष्ट्रनिनदोपमैः ।\nआहुरन्योन्यमुक्तानि प्रब्रुवाणा मदोत्कटाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With various drunken songs like the braying of donkeys and the cries of camels, they say to each other wild words, swollen with intoxication."}},{"n":18,"text":"हा हते हा हतेत्येव स्वामिभर्तृहतेति च ।\nआक्रोशन्त्यः प्रनृत्यन्ति मन्दाः पर्वस्वसंयताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ha, I am struck! Ha, struck!\" they cry, and \"My master's wife is struck!\", dancing foolish and unrestrained on festival days."}},{"n":19,"text":"तेषां किलावलिप्तानां निवसन्कुरुजाङ्गले ।\nकश्चिद्बाह्लीकमुख्यानां नातिहृष्टमना जगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is said that a certain leading Bahlika among those proud people, living in the Kuru country, sang with a heavy heart:"}},{"n":20,"text":"सा नूनं बृहती गौरी सूक्ष्मकम्बलवासिनी ।\nमामनुस्मरती शेते बाह्लीकं कुरुवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely she, tall and fair, in her fine blanket, lies remembering me, the Bahlika living among the Kurus.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"शतद्रुकनदीं तीर्त्वा तां च रम्यामिरावतीम् ।\nगत्वा स्वदेशं द्रक्ष्यामि स्थूलशङ्खाः शुभाः स्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Crossing the river Shatadru and the lovely Iravati, and reaching my own country, I shall see the women with big conch-shell bracelets.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"मनःशिलोज्ज्वलापाङ्गा गौर्यस्त्रिककुदाञ्जनाः ।\nकेवलाजिनसंवीताः कूर्दन्त्यः प्रियदर्शनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fair women with bright eyes outlined in red arsenic, with collyrium on the three-peaked head, wrapped only in hides, leaping about, lovely to see.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"मृदङ्गानकशङ्खानां मर्दलानां च निस्वनैः ।\nखरोष्ट्राश्वतरैश्चैव मत्ता यास्यामहे सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With the sounds of drums, tabors, conches and mridangas, drunk, riding donkeys, camels and mules, we will go happily.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"शमीपीलुकरीराणां वनेषु सुखवर्त्मसु ।\nअपूपान्सक्तुपिण्डीश्च खादन्तो मथितान्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Along pleasant paths through forests of shami, pilu and kari trees, eating cakes and balls of barley meal with buttermilk,\""}},{"n":25,"text":"पथिषु प्रबला भूत्वा कदासमृदितेऽध्वनि ।\nखलोपहारं कुर्वाणास्ताडयिष्याम भूयसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"growing strong on the roads, on the trodden way, bringing offerings of dregs, we shall beat many more.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"एवं हीनेषु व्रात्येषु बाह्लीकेषु दुरात्मसु ।\nकश्चेतयानो निवसेन्मुहूर्तमपि मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among such low, outcast, evil-souled Bahlikas, what thinking man would live even for a moment?"}},{"n":27,"text":"ईदृशा ब्राह्मणेनोक्ता बाह्लीका मोघचारिणः ।\nयेषां षड्भागहर्ता त्वमुभयोः शुभपापयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such Bahlikas, whose conduct is futile, were described by that brahmin; and you take a sixth share of both their merit and their sin."}},{"n":28,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा ब्राह्मणः साधुरुत्तरं पुनरुक्तवान् ।\nबाह्लीकेष्वविनीतेषु प्रोच्यमानं निबोधत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the good brahmin spoke again; hear what he said of the undisciplined Bahlikas."}},{"n":29,"text":"तत्र स्म राक्षसी गाति सदा कृष्णचतुर्दशीम् ।\nनगरे शाकले स्फीते आहत्य निशि दुन्दुभिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There a she-demon always sings on the fourteenth of the dark fortnight, beating a drum at night in the prosperous city of Shakala."}},{"n":30,"text":"कदा वा घोषिका गाथाः पुनर्गास्यन्ति शाकले ।\nगव्यस्य तृप्ता मांसस्य पीत्वा गौडं महासवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When will the herald women sing their songs again in Shakala, full of beef, drinking great gaudy liquor of molasses,\""}},{"n":31,"text":"गौरीभिः सह नारीभिर्बृहतीभिः स्वलंकृताः ।\nपलाण्डुगण्डूषयुतान्खादन्ते चैडकान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"with fair, tall women, well adorned, eating many sheep along with mouthfuls of onions?\""}},{"n":32,"text":"वाराहं कौक्कुटं मांसं गव्यं गार्दभमौष्ट्रकम् ।\nऐडं च ये न खादन्ति तेषां जन्म निरर्थकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who do not eat pork, chicken, beef, donkey, camel and mutton: their birth is in vain.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"इति गायन्ति ये मत्ताः शीधुना शाकलावतः ।\nसबालवृद्धाः कूर्दन्तस्तेषु वृत्तं कथं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So sing the Shakala people, drunk on liquor; with children and elders alike leaping about, what conduct could they have?"}},{"n":34,"text":"इति शल्य विजानीहि हन्त भूयो ब्रवीमि ते ।\nयदन्योऽप्युक्तवानस्मान्ब्राह्मणः कुरुसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this, Shalya; and I will tell you more, for another brahmin also said something about us in the Kuru assembly."}},{"n":35,"text":"पञ्च नद्यो वहन्त्येता यत्र पीलुवनान्यपि ।\nशतद्रुश्च विपाशा च तृतीयेरावती तथा ।\nचन्द्रभागा वितस्ता च सिन्धुषष्ठा बहिर्गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where these five rivers flow with their groves of pilu trees, the Shatadru, the Vipasha, third the Iravati, the Chandrabhaga, the Vitasta, with the Sindhu as sixth, those outside the pale live."}},{"n":36,"text":"आरट्टा नाम ते देशा नष्टधर्मान्न तान्व्रजेत् ।\nव्रात्यानां दासमीयानां विदेहानामयज्वनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those countries called Aratta have lost dharma; one should not go there: the land of outcasts, of the Dasamiyas, of the Videhas who do not sacrifice."}},{"n":37,"text":"न देवाः प्रतिगृह्णन्ति पितरो ब्राह्मणास्तथा ।\nतेषां प्रनष्टधर्माणां बाह्लीकानामिति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, ancestors and brahmins do not accept anything from those Bahlikas who have lost dharma, so the tradition says."}},{"n":38,"text":"ब्राह्मणेन तथा प्रोक्तं विदुषा साधुसंसदि ।\nकाष्ठकुण्डेषु बाह्लीका मृण्मयेषु च भुञ्जते ।\nसक्तुवाट्यावलिप्तेषु श्वादिलीढेषु निर्घृणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A learned brahmin said this in a good assembly: the Bahlikas eat from wooden bowls and clay dishes, smeared with barley-paste and licked by dogs, merciless."}},{"n":39,"text":"आविकं चौष्ट्रिकं चैव क्षीरं गार्दभमेव च ।\nतद्विकारांश्च बाह्लीकाः खादन्ति च पिबन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Bahlikas eat and drink sheep's, camel's and donkey's milk and what is made from it."}},{"n":40,"text":"पुत्रसंकरिणो जाल्माः सर्वान्नक्षीरभोजनाः ।\nआरट्टा नाम बाह्लीका वर्जनीया विपश्चिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are mixed in their sons, base, eat all kinds of food and milk; the Bahlikas called Arattas are to be avoided by the wise."}},{"n":41,"text":"उत शल्य विजानीहि हन्त भूयो ब्रवीमि ते ।\nयदन्योऽप्युक्तवान्सभ्यो ब्राह्मणः कुरुसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this too, Shalya; I will say more, for another man of the assembly, a brahmin, spoke in the Kuru court."}},{"n":42,"text":"युगंधरे पयः पीत्वा प्रोष्य चाप्यच्युतस्थले ।\nतद्वद्भूतिलये स्नात्वा कथं स्वर्गं गमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who has drunk milk at Yugandhara, stayed at Achyutasthala and bathed at Bhutilaya: how will he go to heaven?\""}},{"n":43,"text":"पञ्च नद्यो वहन्त्येता यत्र निःसृत्य पर्वतात् ।\nआरट्टा नाम बाह्लीका न तेष्वार्यो द्व्यहं वसेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where these five rivers flow out of the mountain, there are the Arattas, called Bahlikas; a noble man should not live even two days in them."}},{"n":44,"text":"बहिश्च नाम ह्लीकश्च विपाशायां पिशाचकौ ।\nतयोरपत्यं बाह्लीका नैषा सृष्टिः प्रजापतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahis and Hlika were two pishachas on the Vipasha; the Bahlikas are their offspring; this is not a creation of Prajapati."}},{"n":45,"text":"कारस्करान्महिषकान्कलिङ्गान्कीकटाटवीन् ।\nकर्कोटकान्वीरकांश्च दुर्धर्मांश्च विवर्जयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should avoid the Karaskaras, Mahishakas, Kalingas, Kikata forests, Karkotakas, Virakas and the evil-dharma people."}},{"n":46,"text":"इति तीर्थानुसर्तारं राक्षसी काचिदब्रवीत् ।\nएकरात्रा शमीगेहे महोलूखलमेखला ॥","meaning":{"en":"So a certain she-demon said to a man who was visiting holy places, a night in the shami house, wearing a great mortar as girdle."}},{"n":47,"text":"आरट्टा नाम ते देशा बाह्लीका नाम ते जनाः ।\nवसातिसिन्धुसौवीरा इति प्रायो विकुत्सिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those countries are called Aratta, those people Bahlika; Vasati, Sindhu and Sauvira are mostly reviled."}},{"n":48,"text":"उत शल्य विजानीहि हन्त भूयो ब्रवीमि ते ।\nउच्यमानं मया सम्यक्तदेकाग्रमनाः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this too, Shalya; I will say more; listen with a single mind to what I say rightly."}},{"n":49,"text":"ब्राह्मणः शिल्पिनो गेहमभ्यगच्छत्पुरातिथिः ।\nआचारं तत्र संप्रेक्ष्य प्रीतः शिल्पिनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin once came as a guest to a craftsman's house; seeing the conduct there, he was pleased and said to the craftsman:"}},{"n":50,"text":"मया हिमवतः शृङ्गमेकेनाध्युषितं चिरम् ।\nदृष्टाश्च बहवो देशा नानाधर्मसमाकुलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I once lived long on a peak of the Himalaya, alone, and saw many countries filled with different customs.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"न च केन च धर्मेण विरुध्यन्ते प्रजा इमाः ।\nसर्वे हि तेऽब्रुवन्धर्मं यथोक्तं वेदपारगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And these peoples did not contradict each other in any dharma; all of them spoke of dharma as stated by those who have mastered the Vedas.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"अटता तु सदा देशान्नानाधर्मसमाकुलान् ।\nआगच्छता महाराज बाह्लीकेषु निशामितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But, great king, in always wandering through lands full of various customs, I observed this when I came among the Bahlikas.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तत्रैव ब्राह्मणो भूत्वा ततो भवति क्षत्रियः ।\nवैश्यः शूद्रश्च बाह्लीकस्ततो भवति नापितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There one is first a brahmin, then becomes a kshatriya, a vaishya, a shudra, then a Bahlika, then a barber.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"नापितश्च ततो भूत्वा पुनर्भवति ब्राह्मणः ।\nद्विजो भूत्वा च तत्रैव पुनर्दासोऽपि जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having become a barber, he becomes a brahmin again; having been twice-born, he is born a servant there again.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"भवत्येकः कुले विप्रः शिष्टान्ये कामचारिणः ।\nगान्धारा मद्रकाश्चैव बाह्लीकाः केऽप्यचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In a family there is one brahmin, and the rest do as they like: Gandharas, Madrakas, Bahlikas, some witless.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"एतन्मया श्रुतं तत्र धर्मसंकरकारकम् ।\nकृत्स्नामटित्वा पृथिवीं बाह्लीकेषु विपर्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This I heard there, the cause of mixing of dharma; having wandered the whole earth, I found reversal among the Bahlikas.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"उत शल्य विजानीहि हन्त भूयो ब्रवीमि ते ।\nयदप्यन्योऽब्रवीद्वाक्यं बाह्लीकानां विकुत्सितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this too, Shalya; I will say more, for another man also said a reviling word of the Bahlikas."}},{"n":58,"text":"सती पुरा हृता काचिदारट्टा किल दस्युभिः ।\nअधर्मतश्चोपयाता सा तानभ्यशपत्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say a good woman of the Arattas was once carried off by robbers and approached against dharma, and she cursed them."}},{"n":59,"text":"बालां बन्धुमतीं यन्मामधर्मेणोपगच्छथ ।\nतस्मान्नार्यो भविष्यन्ति बन्धक्यो वै कुलेषु वः ।\nन चैवास्मात्प्रमोक्ष्यध्वं घोरात्पापान्नराधमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Since you violate me, a young girl with kin, against dharma, the women of your families will be loose, and you, lowest of men, will not be freed from this dreadful sin.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"कुरवः सहपाञ्चालाः शाल्वा मत्स्याः सनैमिषाः ।\nकोसलाः काशयोऽङ्गाश्च कलिङ्गा मगधास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus with the Panchalas, the Shalvas, Matsyas with the Naimishas, Kosalas, Kashis, Angas, Kalingas and Magadhas,"}},{"n":61,"text":"चेदयश्च महाभागा धर्मं जानन्ति शाश्वतम् ।\nनानादेशेषु सन्तश्च प्रायो बाह्या लयादृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the exalted Chedis know eternal dharma; in many countries there are good people, but mostly outsiders except for the Layas."}},{"n":62,"text":"आ मत्स्येभ्यः कुरुपाञ्चालदेश्या\nआ नैमिषाच्चेदयो ये विशिष्टाः ।\nधर्मं पुराणमुपजीवन्ति सन्तो\nमद्रानृते पञ्चनदांश्च जिह्मान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the Matsyas on, the people of the Kuru-Panchala land and, from Naimisha, the best Chedis, good people live by ancient dharma, except the Madras and the crooked five-river people."}},{"n":63,"text":"एवं विद्वन्धर्मकथांश्च राजं-\nस्तूष्णींभूतो जडवच्छल्य भूयाः ।\nत्वं तस्य गोप्ता च जनस्य राजा\nषड्भागहर्ता शुभदुष्कृतस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing so, king, and these talks of dharma, Shalya, be silent as if dull. You are the guardian of those people and their king, taking a sixth of their good and evil."}},{"n":64,"text":"अथ वा दुष्कृतस्य त्वं हर्ता तेषामरक्षिता ।\nरक्षिता पुण्यभाग्राजा प्रजानां त्वं त्वपुण्यभाक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or rather you take their evil deeds and do not protect them; a protecting king shares the merit of his subjects, but you share demerit."}},{"n":65,"text":"पूज्यमाने पुरा धर्मे सर्वदेशेषु शाश्वते ।\nधर्मं पाञ्चनदं दृष्ट्वा धिगित्याह पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When eternal dharma was honored in all lands, the Grandfather, seeing the five-river dharma, said \"Fie.\""}},{"n":66,"text":"व्रात्यानां दाशमीयानां कृतेऽप्यशुभकर्मणाम् ।\nइति पाञ्चनदं धर्ममवमेने पितामहः ।\nस्वधर्मस्थेषु वर्णेषु सोऽप्येतं नाभिपूजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even in the Krita age, of the outcasts, the Dasamiyas, and the evildoers, the Grandfather despised the five-river dharma; and he would not honor it among the varnas who stand in their own duty."}},{"n":67,"text":"उत शल्य विजानीहि हन्त भूयो ब्रवीमि ते ।\nकल्माषपादः सरसि निमज्जन्राक्षसोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this too, Shalya; I will say more: the rakshasa Kalmashapada, sinking in a lake, spoke."}},{"n":68,"text":"क्षत्रियस्य मलं भैक्षं ब्राह्मणस्यानृतं मलम् ।\nमलं पृथिव्या बाह्लीकाः स्त्रीणां मद्रस्त्रियो मलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The kshatriya's stain is begging, the brahmin's stain is lying; the stain of the earth is the Bahlikas, the stain of women is Madra women.\""}},{"n":69,"text":"निमज्जमानमुद्धृत्य कश्चिद्राजा निशाचरम् ।\nअपृच्छत्तेन चाख्यातं प्रोक्तवान्यन्निबोध तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A certain king, having lifted the night-roamer from the water as he sank, questioned him, and what he told, hear now."}},{"n":70,"text":"मानुषाणां मलं म्लेच्छा म्लेच्छानां मौष्टिका मलम् ।\nमौष्टिकानां मलं शण्डाः शण्डानां राजयाजकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The stain of men is barbarians; of barbarians, the Maushtikas; of Maushtikas, eunuchs; of eunuchs, the priests of kings.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"राजयाजकयाज्यानां मद्रकाणां च यन्मलम् ।\nतद्भवेद्वै तव मलं यद्यस्मान्न विमुञ्चसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And what is the stain of the priests' sacrificers and of the Madrakas, that would be your stain too, if you do not release us.\""}},{"n":72,"text":"इति रक्षोपसृष्टेषु विषवीर्यहतेषु च ।\nराक्षसं भेषजं प्रोक्तं संसिद्धं वचनोत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So for those afflicted by demons or struck by the force of poison, the rakshasa's remedy, effective by its final word, was proclaimed."}},{"n":73,"text":"ब्राह्मं पाञ्चालाः कौरवेयाः स्वधर्मः\nसत्यं मत्स्याः शूरसेनाश्च यज्ञः ।\nप्राच्या दासा वृषला दाक्षिणात्याः\nस्तेना बाह्लीकाः संकरा वै सुराष्ट्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas follow Brahma, the Kauravas their own dharma, the Matsyas truth, the Shurasenas sacrifice; the Easterners are servants, southerners outcasts, Bahlikas thieves, and Surashtras mixed."}},{"n":74,"text":"कृतघ्नता परवित्तापहारः\nसुरापानं गुरुदारावमर्शः ।\nयेषां धर्मस्तान्प्रति नास्त्यधर्म\nआरट्टकान्पाञ्चनदान्धिगस्तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ingratitude, taking others' property, drinking liquor, touching a teacher's wife: for those whose dharma is these, there is no wrong. Fie on the Arattakas and the five-river people!"}},{"n":75,"text":"आ पाञ्चालेभ्यः कुरवो नैमिषाश्च\nमत्स्याश्चैवाप्यथ जानन्ति धर्मम् ।\nकलिङ्गकाश्चाङ्गका मागधाश्च\nशिष्टान्धर्मानुपजीवन्ति वृद्धाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the Panchalas on, the Kurus, Naimishas, Matsyas know dharma, and the Kalingas, Angas and Magadhas, being elders, live by the dharma of the good."}},{"n":76,"text":"प्राचीं दिशं श्रिता देवा जातवेदःपुरोगमाः ।\nदक्षिणां पितरो गुप्तां यमेन शुभकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods dwell in the eastern direction, led by Agni; the ancestors in the south, guarded by Yama of good deeds."}},{"n":77,"text":"प्रतीचीं वरुणः पाति पालयन्नसुरान्बली ।\nउदीचीं भगवान्सोमो ब्रह्मण्यो ब्राह्मणैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Varuna protects the west, keeping the asuras in check, the mighty one; in the north the blessed Soma, friend of brahmins, with the brahmins."}},{"n":78,"text":"रक्षःपिशाचान्हिमवान्गुह्यकान्गन्धमादनः ।\nध्रुवः सर्वाणि भूतानि विष्णुर्लोकाञ्जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Himalaya guards rakshasas and pishachas; Gandhamadana, the guhyakas; Dhruva all beings; Vishnu Janardana the worlds."}},{"n":79,"text":"इङ्गितज्ञाश्च मगधाः प्रेक्षितज्ञाश्च कोसलाः ।\nअर्धोक्ताः कुरुपाञ्चालाः शाल्वाः कृत्स्नानुशासनाः ।\nपार्वतीयाश्च विषमा यथैव गिरयस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Magadhas understand hints, the Kosalas glances, the Kuru-Panchalas half-said words, the Shalvas need complete instruction; the mountain people are rough like their mountains."}},{"n":80,"text":"सर्वज्ञा यवना राजञ्शूराश्चैव विशेषतः ।\nम्लेच्छाः स्वसंज्ञानियता नानुक्त इतरो जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Yavanas, king, know everything, and the brave especially; the barbarians stay with their own signs; no one else needs telling."}},{"n":81,"text":"प्रतिरब्धास्तु बाह्लीका न च केचन मद्रकाः ।\nस त्वमेतादृशः शल्य नोत्तरं वक्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the Bahlikas are stubborn, and none are Madrakas. Such as you are, Shalya, you should not answer."}},{"n":82,"text":"एतज्ज्ञात्वा जोषमास्स्व प्रतीपं मा स्म वै कृथाः ।\nस त्वां पूर्वमहं हत्वा हनिष्ये केशवार्जुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, keep silent, do not oppose me. I shall kill you first, and then kill Keshava and Arjuna."}},{"text":"शल्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shalya said:"}},{"n":83,"text":"आतुराणां परित्यागः स्वदारसुतविक्रयः ।\nअङ्गेषु वर्तते कर्ण येषामधिपतिर्भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, abandoning the afflicted and selling one's wife and sons goes on among the Angas, whose lord you are."}},{"n":84,"text":"रथातिरथसंख्यायां यत्त्वा भीष्मस्तदाब्रवीत् ।\nतान्विदित्वात्मनो दोषान्निर्मन्युर्भव मा क्रुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know the faults in yourself that Bhishma told you when he counted the rathas and atirathas, and be free from anger; do not rage."}},{"n":85,"text":"सर्वत्र ब्राह्मणाः सन्ति सन्ति सर्वत्र क्षत्रियाः ।\nवैश्याः शूद्रास्तथा कर्ण स्त्रियः साध्व्यश्च सुव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everywhere there are brahmins, everywhere kshatriyas, vaishyas and shudras, Karna, and women who are good and keep their vows."}},{"n":86,"text":"रमन्ते चोपहासेन पुरुषाः पुरुषैः सह ।\nअन्योन्यमवतक्षन्तो देशे देशे समैथुनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men also amuse themselves with jests, with other men, mocking one another, and in every land there is lewdness."}},{"n":87,"text":"परवाच्येषु निपुणः सर्वो भवति सर्वदा ।\nआत्मवाच्यं न जानीते जानन्नपि विमुह्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everyone is always skilled in others' faults; he does not know his own, or if he knows, he is bewildered."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":88,"text":"कर्णोऽपि नोत्तरं प्राह शल्योऽप्यभिमुखः परान् ।\nपुनः प्रहस्य राधेयः पुनर्याहीत्यचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna gave no reply, and Shalya, facing the enemies, was silent too. Radheya laughed again and urged him: \"Drive on again!\""}}]}]}